  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-openmaic",
      "text": "把 OpenMAIC 带进 DeepSeek Harness。Bring OpenMAIC into DeepSeek Harness.\n\n`dsh-openmaic` is a DeepSeek Harness plugin that registers four tools and a\nSocratic teaching skill:"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-openmaic",
      "text": "- `openmaic_generate`: tell your agent \"make me a lesson about X\", and the plugin submits the requirement to [open.maic.chat](https://open.maic.chat/), waits for the async generation job, and returns a playable classroom link.\n- `openmaic_slide`: the agent writes one OpenMAIC slide (PPTist-style Slide JSON) and the plugin renders it with OpenMAIC's official renderer (text, shapes, images, tables, charts, formulas, code).\n- `openmaic_widget`: the agent writes an OpenMAIC-style interactive widget (simulation, game, or code) per the bundled contract; the code streams as it writes, then renders inline as a sandboxed card.\n- `openmaic_render`: the agent writes an inline HTML teaching fragment (concept card, quiz, walkthrough) and the plugin renders it as a sandboxed card right in the conversation.\n- `openmaic-teach` skill: turns a session into a Socratic OpenMAIC lesson, teaching by guided questioning and pulling in slides, widgets, and cards as aids."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it looks like",
      "text": "```\n用户: 帮我做一节量子物理入门课\n模型 → openmaic_generate(requirement=\"量子物理入门课\", language=\"zh-CN\")\n     ← \"Classroom ID: class-abc123\n        Classroom URL:\n\nInteractive widget:\n\n```\n用户: 做一个抛体运动模拟器\n模型 → 按 openmaic-widget 模板写完整 HTML（流式输出）\n     → openmaic_widget(html=\"<!doctype html>…\", widgetType=\"simulation\", title=\"抛体运动\")\n     ← \"Rendered the simulation widget …\""
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add git+https://github.com/THU-MAIC/dsh-openmaic.git\n```\n\nThen restart `dsh web` and refresh. The plugin ships its compiled `lib/`, so a\ngit install needs no build step."
    },
    {
      "section": "Config",
      "text": "```yaml\ndsh-openmaic:\n  baseUrl: https://open.maic.chat\n  accessCode: \"\"     # invite code; not enforced online yet, leave empty\n  pollIntervalMs: 5000"
    },
    {
      "section": "Config",
      "text": "| Key | Default | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `baseUrl` | `https://open.maic.chat` | API base. Point at `http://localhost:3000` to develop against a local OpenMAIC. |\n| `accessCode` | `\"\"` | Invite code for open.maic.chat. Not enforced online yet, leave empty; fill it in once enabled. |\n| `pollIntervalMs` | `5000` | Poll interval in ms. Generation is slow, so 60000 is friendlier than the default. |\n| `maxWaitMs` | `600000` | Cap for one job, 10 minutes. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "API flow",
      "text": "1. If `accessCode` is set, `POST /api/access-code/verify` and replay the `openmaic_access` cookie on later requests.\n2. `POST /api/generate-classroom` with the requirement, plus only the optional flags you passed. Returns a `jobId` and `pollUrl`.\n3. Poll `GET {pollUrl}` until the job is `succeeded` or `failed`, or `maxWaitMs` runs out.\n4. On success, return `{baseUrl}/classroom/{classroomId}` (or the server-provided `result.url`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Scope",
      "text": "- `openmaic_generate`: generate a classroom and return a playable link.\n- `openmaic_slide`: render one OpenMAIC slide with the official renderer.\n- `openmaic_widget`: render a simulation / game / code widget the agent writes (a full HTML document). It streams the code while the agent writes it and renders on completion.\n- `openmaic_render`: render an inline HTML teaching fragment as a sandboxed card.\n- `openmaic-teach`: Socratic teaching session that uses the tools above as aids."
    },
    {
      "section": "Scope",
      "text": "The slide/widget/render tools do no server-side generation; they render content\nthe agent authors against the OpenMAIC SDK contracts (`@openmaic/dsl`,\n`@openmaic/generation`, `@openmaic/renderer`)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Roadmap",
      "text": "- Wire the remaining widget types (diagram, visualization3d, procedural-skill).\n- Action loop back to the model (teaching-agent interactions: highlight/annotate/reveal widget elements)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\n./scripts/build.sh  # links host deps, bundles src/ to lib/ with tsdown\n./scripts/test.sh   # links host deps, runs the vitest suite\n```\n\nThe scripts locate the harness checkout from `dsh` on `PATH`; set `DSH_CHECKOUT` to build against a specific checkout."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT"
    }
  ],
